{"title":"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many zeros does <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca23936130e9163faf591256d872bfaed0c15cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\cos(\\log x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" /> have on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4f17e1346c7c9bb4f51a1dc76b4e547a9da487c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/212481eb725ff7eb49e7a884bfdac50662557d62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 0 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 1 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 10 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\text{infinitely\\ many}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"451\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4f17e1346c7c9bb4f51a1dc76b4e547a9da487c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae29662603d1c9f06310a153d6c8dc55ba7e50eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\infty &lt; \\log x &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />, and the logarithm is a strictly increasing function on this interval.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/d/65d5859dd6226d24232ec85a9c5ee32a7312e95b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> is zero for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e166562301e0106c5a9c8802ad6906a66131a180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}2 + k\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"58\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/5586db7ead68a6ecd88ebc290818d5f1f5309e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39aa33a8b7f2cf52a1c9815264fa309a1a94d40c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{infinitely\\ many}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"121\" height=\"26\" /> such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/0/de039d7988e740b7c08b2004f4478cb5ddad055a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-\\infty,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Here's the graph of the function on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf2431375372a86356755fa21f598ca5a41c2d7c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  size(250,200,IgnoreAspect);  real f(real t) {return cos(log(t));}  draw(graph(f,0.01,1),red,&quot;$\\cos(\\log(x))$&quot;);  xaxis(&quot;$x$&quot;,BottomTop,LeftTicks); yaxis(&quot;$y$&quot;,LeftRight,RightTicks(trailingzero));  attach(legend(),truepoint(E),20E,UnFill); [/asy]\" width=\"665\" height=\"338\" />\n</p><p>As we go closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the function will more and more wildly oscilate between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This is how it looks like at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a70a15c4d22c46a9d074211a3ab6efdeb49d7df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0.0001,0.02)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c2598278cc59119edb942ef4a3b8c14f08f8ce70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  size(250,200,IgnoreAspect);  real f(real t) {return cos(log(t));}  draw(graph(f,0.0001,0.02),red,&quot;$\\cos(\\log(x))$&quot;);  xaxis(&quot;$x$&quot;,BottomTop,LeftTicks); yaxis(&quot;$y$&quot;,LeftRight,RightTicks(trailingzero));  attach(legend(),truepoint(E),20E,UnFill); [/asy]\" width=\"655\" height=\"335\" />\n</p><p>And one more zoom, at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d364027264032541e31b4c6139e187a125900692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0.000001,0.0005)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aed9faa016e21438c773ea933f787f5e39ef94bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  size(250,200,IgnoreAspect);  real f(real t) {return cos(log(t));}  draw(graph(f,0.000001,0.0005),red,&quot;$\\cos(\\log(x))$&quot;);  xaxis(&quot;$x$&quot;,BottomTop,LeftTicks); yaxis(&quot;$y$&quot;,LeftRight,RightTicks(trailingzero));  attach(legend(),truepoint(E),20E,UnFill); [/asy]\" width=\"648\" height=\"335\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If cos(log(x)) = zero, then log(x) = π/2 + nπ.\n</p><p>If we consider the limiting case as x approaches zero, log(x) approaches negative infinity. \n</p><p>If we consider the other boundary, x equals 1 where log(x) equals zero.\n</p><p>Due to the intermediate value theorem log(x) must contain all negative real numbers, and thus an infinite number of solutions to log(x) = π/2 + nπ.\nThis means that cos(x) is zero an infinite number of times giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/8/b180ecd068e10174bfbd23f556791d712e8a7565.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E) infinitely\\ many}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"152\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-PhysicsMan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME\" title=\"1999 AHSME\">1999 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_